          <div type="commentary">
            <p>I have encoded gaps in two different ways -- the gaps without specific quantities indicate the text that would have existed outside of the available fragments. The gaps with quantities are based on either illegible characters or gaps for which the quantity of characters can be conjectured based on 
            the physical form of the inscription.</p>
              
            <p>Encoding each fragment as a separate text part means the numbering of the lines differs significantly from the edition in <ptr target="bib:Krishnamacharlu1940_01"/> who edited the four fragments without interruption in the line numbers.</p>  
         </div>
      
